# gitleaks false positives that .gitleaks.toml's rules cannot describe, one
# fingerprint per verified finding. Prefer a rule in .gitleaks.toml (it does
# not move when a line moves) or an inline `gitleaks:allow` comment; use this
# file only for a file that can carry neither. Each line is triaged in
# docs/security/scanner-triage.md#gitleaks — read the row before adding one.
# Fingerprint shape for a filesystem scan is path:rule:line, so a line that
# moves needs its fingerprint moved with it.
#
# The content-manifest Firebase links and the NewsletterConfirmPage test
# fixture that used to be listed here are covered by .gitleaks.toml since
# the Qlty security clean-up of 2026-11-24.

# The Azure Cosmos DB emulator's published well-known key, against localhost.
# JSON cannot carry an inline comment, and an allowlist keyed on an .example
# file name would also wave through a real key pasted into one.
functions/local.settings.json.example:generic-api-key:7
